### Exploratory endpoints

::: {.content-visible when-meta="tier-longitudinal"}
- **CRI-Opioid trajectory over 12 months** in the longitudinal sub-study, against concurrent opioid wanting ratings and toxicology (@sec-longitudinal-substudy).
- **Repetition and habituation effects**, modeling presentation number and repetition lag across repeated exposure to a fixed image set. This is a condition of running the sub-study rather than an optional extension of it: without it, an attenuating CRI-Opioid cannot be distinguished from habituation to the stimuli, and a fielded device would read the second as treatment response.
:::

- **CRI-Opioid by MOUD type**, contingent on sufficient enrollment in each stratum.

::: {.content-visible when-meta="tier-longitudinal"}
- **Within-person CRI-Opioid change against subsequent toxicology**, as groundwork toward a future monitoring argument. No monitoring claim is made and none is supported by this design.
:::

- Drug-wanting burden on the Opioid Craving Scale (OCS), [Patient Global Impression of Change (PGIC), benzodiazepine]{.content-visible when-meta="tier-outcomes"}[benzodiazepine]{.content-visible unless-meta="tier-outcomes"} (BNZ) analyte, pre- to post-task change in drug wanting, and PROMIS-29 subscales other than Sleep Disturbance, all descriptive.

